  "claim_boundary": "This receipt proves two fresh local executions of the four relevant engines rebuild the committed directory and deterministic ZIP bytes from two locked pre-decision G.19 revolving-credit table values in one April 7 archived Federal Reserve PDF. It verifies the separately locked March value is disjoint and, as an evaluation only, falls 3,550 basis points below the previously declared no-probability range. The range is not widened after the fact, and the May release's 100-basis-point downward revisions to January and February do not overwrite the decision snapshot. The G.19 table values are simple annual rates calculated from unrounded data and are not replaced with rounded headline fractions. This does not prove forecast skill, calibrated coverage, household, card-spending, consumer, pandemic, policy, lender, or macroeconomic causality, investment performance, deployment, external review, or user impact.",
